.ct-header
  display: flex
  padding: 0 0.25em;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;

#isonim-debug-controls
  // The caption bar's left region drags; the control row inside it does not.
  //
  // This element is not the toolbar — it is the bar's left THIRD.  `#menu` gives
  // it `flex: 1 1 0` so it takes an equal share of the leftover space with the
  // session tab bar, which is what centres the command prompt between them (see
  // components/menu_bar.styl).  So it is as wide as the tab strip opposite —
  // ~887px on this display — while the buttons it holds come to ~520px.
  //
  // Marking this container `no-drag` therefore froze the whole 887px, including
  // the ~367px of empty bar after the last button.  That is why the gap left of
  // the command prompt would not move the window while the identical gap on its
  // right would: the tab bar opposite has had the other arrangement all along
  // (components/session_tabs.styl — "Empty bar area is draggable; child
  // tabs/buttons override with no-drag").
  //
  // The opt-out is scoped to the direct child rather than to the buttons so the
  // hole is exactly the control row: it then tracks the row's width by itself
  // when buttons are added or removed, and the gaps between buttons stay
  // non-draggable, so missing a button by a pixel does not drag the window.
  -webkit-app-region: drag
  display: flex
  align-items: center
  align-self: center
  flex: 0 0 auto
  order: 2

  > *
    -webkit-app-region: no-drag

  .isonim-debug-controls
    height: 2.1em
    gap: 0.5em
    padding: 0

    .debug-toolbar-mode,
    .recording-head-indicator
      display: inline-flex
      align-items: center
      height: 100%
      padding: 0 0.35em
      font-size: 0.8em
      line-height: 1
      white-space: nowrap
      color: colors-ui-text-primary-body

    .recording-head-indicator
      color: PRIMARY_COLOR

    .jump-to-live-debug
      min-width: 2.8em
      padding: 0 0.35em
      font-size: 0.78em
      line-height: 1
